{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-1209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which statement is **not** true?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-1209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z⊆{Z}^{+}$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a positive integer. For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin {Z}^{+}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-1209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1"} {"question" "q-1209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-1209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N⊆Z"] ["math" "Z⊆Z"] ["math" "Z⊆{Z}^{+}"] ["math" "{Z}^{+}⊆Z"] ["math" "{Z}^{-}⊆Z"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-1209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Z⊆{Z}^{+}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all of the subsets of $A={-1,1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/assets/6c08214e0ec5c2700561f9162c263c9677c621ff240823c261ce446dde38486a.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set, since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{-1},{1},{-1,1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-1},{-1,1}"] ["math" "{-1},{1},{-1,0}"] ["math" "{0},{-1},{1},{-1,1}"] ["math" "∅,{-1},{1},{-1,1}"] ["math" "∅,{1},{1,2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37258" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅,{-1},{1},{-1,1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={2{n}^{2}∣n\\in N,1\\le n\\le 3}$ and $B={2,0,8,18}?$ \n\n- $A⊈B$\n- $∅⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊇B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {1,2,3}$ into the formula $2{n}^{2},$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=1 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {1}^{2}=2 \\\\ n=2 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2}=8 \\\\ n=3 & \\,⇒\\,2\\cdot {3}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA={2,8,18}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊈B$ is false. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $∅⊆B$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is false. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "II, III and IV only"] ["text" "III and IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-37261" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find all of the subsets of $S={r,t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find every subset of $S,$ we list out every combination of elements within $S.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/assets/022399e6a7a5e1f79b58e856aa8e9e5e9f3561e8e4bcb5b80a95237d30d06002.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{r},{t},{r,t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{r,t}"] ["math" "{r},{t}"] ["math" "{r},{t},{r,t}"] ["math" "∅,{r,t}"] ["math" "∅,{r},{t},{r,t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-104924" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅,{r},{t},{r,t}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in Z∣x\\le 5}$ and $B={x\\in Z∣-7\\le x<3}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $B⊈A$\n- $A⊇B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $x\\le 5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={…,-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $-7\\le x<3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={-7,-6,-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false.  For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true, while $B⊈A$ is false. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0667bfe035df587e2031bc104cc8b2f39e4702dc3fe27d88200b2f818d587e1"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III and IV only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"} {"question" "q-105065" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and IV only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070456/state.json" "file_sha256" "a0c1f145fb8cc7dc4c5cb1cfdadc55e6a69ca75d4efba804d95fa1a5e4cecba0"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2484 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
